---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About – Ynvesters AI Tools"
  description="Learn about the Ynvesters AI Editorial Team and our mission to help you find the best AI tools."
>
  <div style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem;">
    <h1 style="font-size:2rem; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">About Ynvesters</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom:2rem; font-size:1.1rem;">
      Your daily guide to the AI tools landscape.
    </p>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        The AI tools ecosystem moves fast — new products launch daily, pricing changes overnight, and yesterday's hot tool is obsolete by next week.
        Ynvesters exists to cut through the noise. We publish daily, in-depth reviews and comparisons so you can make informed decisions without spending hours on research.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        Ynvesters is produced by the <strong>AI Editorial Team</strong> — a research pipeline that combines automated data collection (official docs, GitHub repositories, real user discussions) with structured editorial review.
        Every article is built from primary sources: pricing pages, feature changelogs, and community feedback.
        We do not publish affiliate-first puff pieces. Our goal is accuracy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>What We Cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AI writing assistants, coding tools, image generators, and productivity apps</li>
        <li>Head-to-head tool comparisons with objective criteria</li>
        <li>Pricing and free-tier breakdowns updated when products change</li>
        <li>"How to use" tutorials for new tools</li>
        <li>Weekly roundups of notable AI launches</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
      <p>
        All claims are sourced from official documentation or verifiable third-party sources.
        External links go to primary sources (official sites, GitHub, academic papers) — we do not accept sponsored placement.
        If you spot an error or outdated information, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
